%N A337828 Odd integers k such that 3^((k-1)/2) + 1 == 0 (mod k*(k-1)/2).
%C A337828 Computed terms are prime.
%C A337828 Each term is a prime or Fermat pseudoprime base 3 (A005935). Furthermore, for each term k, (k-1)/2 is a term of A015949. Conjecture: sequence consists of primes p == 2 (mod 3) such that (p-1)/2 is in A015949. - _Max Alekseyev_, Jul 26 2026
%t A337828 Select[Range[3, 3*10^7, 2], PowerMod[3, (# - 1)/2, (t = #*(# - 1)/2)] == t - 1 &] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 24 2020 *)
%Y A337828 Cf. A005935, A015949, A337818.
